      "congressionalglo7392unit:397:par_000397_000018": {
        "text": "Sir, I object at the present time to this whole system of legislation, and the very sensible remarks submitted by the gentleman from Illi- nois [Mr. Wentworth] relieve me from the necessity of an argument upon it. I simply say that I can see no reason as yet in the argument of the chairman of the Committee of Ways and Means or in the remarks from any other quarter of the House for making a distinction between the Canadas and the British Provinces generally, and any other foreign country, in regulating our national tariff.",
